And here is a Java code that can be used to calculate the overall reliability score based on these attributes:
```
public double calculateReliabilityScore(double accuracy, double precision, double recall, double f1Score, double trainingDataQuality, double generalization, double robustness, double speed, double scalability, double explainability) {
    double totalWeight = 0.0;
    double weightedScore = 0.0;
    totalWeight += 0.2;
    weightedScore += accuracy * 0.2;
    totalWeight += 0.1;
    weightedScore += precision * 0.1;
    totalWeight += 0.1;
    weightedScore += recall * 0.1;
    totalWeight += 0.2;
    weightedScore += f1Score * 0.2;
    totalWeight += 0.1;
    weightedScore += trainingDataQuality * 0.1;
    totalWeight += 0.1;
    weightedScore += generalization * 0.1;
    totalWeight += 0.1;
    weightedScore += robustness * 0.1;
    totalWeight += 0.05;
    weightedScore += speed * 0.05;
    totalWeight += 0.05;
    weightedScore += scalability * 0.05;
    totalWeight += 0.05;
    weightedScore += explainability * 0.05;
    return weightedScore / totalWeight;
}
```
